      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/ytc/AIdro_nq1ujPdQHIVfcTYvQJ8AXejYHLogvID_ajD0NgZ11puyy0975KTEngMVn1OBn_mEd1AA=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "Been to Bermuda several times. Absolutely the cleanest safest Island I’ve ever been to. Absolutely beautiful place. Tour guide told us Bermudians work two to three jobs and unemployment is basically non existent  and they have a 99% graduation rate. Said autos can only belong and driven citizens. If one is wrecked it must go to a repair shop and out of site until repaired. He talked about the limestone roofs and rain water storage under every structure. No universities on the island most come to the USA to further their education. Bermuda dollar and the US dollar is always an even exchange and both are accepted by merchants. If you’ve not been there and love visiting island nations Bermuda is a must. I’ve been to many Caribbean Islands but none compare to the cleanliness and safety.  As mentioned Bermuda isn’t a Caribbean Islands it’s in the Atlantic.   Central Tennessee on central time 2:48pm",
